# shell: desktop
# home: fixture
# prefs: factory
# What a first run looks like: the Desktop is Tracker's own, one icon
# leads to the machine's filesystem for whoever wants it, the volumes
# are not poured onto the screen, and the Deskbar lists this shell
# rather than every process the machine happens to run.
wait 20
note one way in to the machine's filesystem, named for the volume it
note opens, as the Disks pose has always been
expect-desk-icon Boot
note the Deskbar knows this shell and nothing it did not start
note the global bar is on, so the leaf sits below it
click 980 40
wait 4
expect-menu Applications
key Escape
wait 4
note and what the screen shows is THAT Desktop, not the login session's
expect-desk-icon notes.txt
note the places a person drops things into are already there
expect-file /tmp/trk_home/.config/tracker/Desktop
expect-file /tmp/trk_home/.config/tracker/icons
